      "source": "manual",
      "category": "architecture",
      "content": "gate-baseline is a FROZEN-REFERENCE, not a pure view (de-commit regression #828→fix #830). The cloud-ci firewall ratchet's frozen baseline is materialized by oya-cloud-ci-scm-facts-emitter-app via `git show <merge-base>:cloud/cloud-ci/gates/oya-cloud-ci-accounting-registry-app/gate-baseline.generated.json` (git_show_file → git cat-file -e). That merge-base extraction REQUIRES the face to be a committed git blob on the main branch (dev). #828/ADR-0595 de-committed it as a \"pure view\" (set materialization_mode: not-tracked-in-git) on the false premise \"the firewall never reads a committed accounting face\" — it does NOT read the working-tree copy but it DOES read the committed blob AT THE MERGE-BASE. Result: git cat-file -e <merge-base>:<path> failed → missing_at_merge_base=true → empty frozen baseline → baseline=0 for every gate code → every pre-existing repo-wide debt item (manifest_missing_version_workspace=55, member_test_code_without_rust_test_target=28, forbidden_foundry=2877, unowned=14253, unjustified=17136, unreachable=12532, ...) reported as a NEW regression on every broad-affected-set PR; PR #829 went RED on buck2 + cloud-ci-firewall. Fix #830: flip materialization_mode back to merge-candidate-regenerated, negate the **/*.generated.json ignore for this one path, re-commit the regenerated face (must include its own scm-facts/unjustified self-row), add the gate-baseline path back to committed scm-facts tracked_paths. The OTHER 5 ADR-0595 faces (accounting-registry, decision-crosswalk, enforcement-inventory, enforcement-liveness, ttl-policy) ARE genuine pure views — their gates re-derive content from the candidate tree, none is pointed at by ratchet-policy.json frozen_reference.face_path — so they correctly STAY de-committed. UNIVERSAL LESSON: the de-commit policy class must distinguish \"frozen-reference baseline (merge-base git-blob materialized)\" from \"pure view (candidate re-derived)\". The tell for frozen-reference: any consumer that reads it via `git show <merge-base>:` — such an artifact MUST stay committed on main. Local buck2 firewall test has a hermetic-sandbox git-state staleness artifact (resolves merge-base to a stale pre-amend ref); the authoritative proof is byte-identity of committed face vs fresh candidate regeneration (current==baseline for every code)."
    }
  ],
